='dialog' element labelled 'Video citation'","when":"the citation modal opens (CitationModal mounts)"},{"given":"an element has keyboard focus in the document and the citation modal is then opened","id":"AC-2","seam":"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect cleanup)","then":"keyboard focus is restored to the element that was focused immediately before the modal opened, when that element remains in the document","when":"the modal closes via any close path (Escape, the Close button, or the backdrop click), unmounting CitationModal"},{"given":"keyboard focus is on a YouTube citation chip rendered by Message in the message list","id":"AC-3","seam":"app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleCitationClick (chip activation opens CitationModal; Escape closes it)","then":"while the modal is open keyboard focus is inside the modal (off the chip), and after Escape the modal is gone and keyboard focus is back on that same citation chip","when":"the chip is activated so the citation modal opens, and the modal is then closed with Escape"},{"given":"the citation modal is open and the element that had focus before it opened has since been removed from the document","id":"AC-4","kind":"guard","seam":"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup)","then":"closing completes without throwing and focus is not forced onto a detached node (document.activeElement falls back to the browser default, body) — the AC's 'when it remains in the document' conditional, pinned so a naive restore cannot regress it","when":"the modal closes"},{"given":"the citation modal is open and keyboard focus is on its Close button (the entry position this change introduces)","id":"AC-5","kind":"guard","seam":"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (document keydown Escape handler)","then":"the modal closes via the existing document keydown handler (onClose invoked) — Escape behaviour is unchanged by the new focus management","when":"Escape is pressed"}],"dependencies":[],"invariants":["Focus entry and return are implemented entirely within CitationModal's own mount/unmount lifecycle (refs plus one mount effect with cleanup); no new props, callbacks or state are added to CitationModal's callers, and ChatArea's conditional mount of CitationModal (ChatArea.tsx:787-789) is unchanged.","The focus effect uses an empty dependency array and does not re-run when the onClose prop identity changes (ChatArea passes a fresh closure every render); re-running on identity churn would re-capture the wrong opener mid-session.","Existing CitationModal tests that pin Escape close, backdrop close, close-button close, iframe embed src with start/autoplay, the 'Open on YouTube' link href and t param, transcript excerpt rendering with pre-wrap, the Video-unavailable states and body-scroll lock remain green without modification.","Dynamous citations never open the modal (ChatArea routes them directly to lesson_url or the missing-link toast), so neither focus criterion ever applies to them.","The Close (×) button keeps rendering unconditionally in every modal state (including Video-unavailable), since focus entry targets it as the only always-present control.","No focus trap, no inert/aria-hidden on background content and no new npm dependency; Tab may still travel from the modal to background content (accepted residual gap, not an acceptance criterion).","Authentication, owner-private conversations and the 25 messages per user per 24 hours limit are untouched."],"issue":{"number":189,"title":"Citation inspection [keyboard]"},"out_of_scope":["Tab containment / focus trap, inert or aria-hidden on background content, and any focus-trap library (the issue forbids new external dependencies and containment is not an acceptance criterion).","The Dynamous citation path (direct lesson_url open and missing-link toast, issue #247).","New content sources, sharing, auth changes, factory authority changes and external dependencies (issue statement).","Modal visual design, video playback, timestamp links and the existing Escape / close-button / backdrop close semantics — preserved behaviour, not redesigned.","Authentication, owner-private conversations and the 25-messages-per-user-per-24-hours limit.","Backend, RAG pipeline and deployment files."],"risks":["React StrictMode (main.tsx) double-invokes effects mount→cleanup→mount in dev; the single empty-deps effect must capture the opener, focus the Close button, and restore in its own cleanup so the simulated remount re-captures the correct opener.","onClose identity churn: ChatArea passes a new closure every render, so keying the focus effect on onClose would re-capture document.activeElement mid-session (the Close button) and corrupt focus-return; reviewers should check the deps array specifically.","jsdom focus semantics: fireEvent.click does not move focus in jsdom, so checkpoints must establish focus with explicit element.focus(); a RED expectation declared from a click-based assumption will not match actual output.","Streaming re-renders can unmount the opener chip while the modal is open, making focus-return no-op to body — this is inside the AC's conditional, not a defect, and is pinned by the opener-removed guard.","Focus entry targets the Close button, which is only correct while it renders unconditionally; today it does, including the Video-unavailable states, and nothing in this build changes that.","Formatter gate: the kernel applies biome format on declared files; keep the new effect's style consistent with AddVideoModal.tsx's focus-on-open effect to avoid burning the hand-back on formatting."],"summary":"Add keyboard focus management to CitationModal: opening the modal moves keyboard focus to the modal's Close button (a usable control inside the dialog), and closing it returns keyboard focus to the element that opened it when that element remains in the document. Implemented entirely within CitationModal's own mount/unmount lifecycle; no changes to callers, close paths, video playback, timestamp links or citation routing.","version":"2.0"},"sha256":"1e4872c41bedc71ca8e0210062d87b20f0b7c8a12d8843d5ada96bdcef2ef63b","source":"task-contract.json"},"design":{"content":{"ac_mapping":{"AC-1":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect with cleanup: focus entry + focus return)"],"AC-2":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect with cleanup: focus entry + focus return)"],"AC-3":["app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleCitationClick (chip activation opens CitationModal; Escape closes it)"],"AC-4":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect with cleanup: focus entry + focus return)"],"AC-5":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (document keydown Escape handler)"]},"allowed_new_files":[],"context_sha256":"674a06476636c493cb59dc93f93505743dff5b622665f990f3e4107dcff7d7fd","contract_sha256":"1e4872c41bedc71ca8e0210062d87b20f0b7c8a12d8843d5ada96bdcef2ef63b","data_flows":["citation chip (native <button> in Message.tsx) -> ChatArea.handleCitationClick -> setSelectedCitation -> CitationModal mounts (ChatArea.tsx:787-789)","document.activeElement at mount -> CitationModal mount effect -> opener captured in effect-local variable, focus moved to Close button ref","Escape keydown / Close button click / backdrop click -> onClose -> CitationModal unmounts -> effect cleanup focuses opener when opener.isConnected, else no-op (focus falls back to body)"],"invariants":["Opening the modal moves keyboard focus to the Close button (role button, accessible name 'Close') inside the role='dialog' element labelled 'Video citation'.","Closing via any path (Escape, Close button, backdrop click) restores focus to the element focused immediately before the modal opened, when that element remains in the document; when it does not, closing completes without throwing and activeElement falls back to the browser default (body).","The focus effect uses an empty dependency array; it never re-runs on onClose identity churn (ChatArea passes a fresh closure every render).","Existing close paths, the document keydown Escape handler, iframe embed src with start/autoplay, the 'Open on YouTube' link, transcript pre-wrap rendering, Video-unavailable states and the body-scroll lock are unchanged.","The Close button keeps rendering unconditionally in every modal state (including Video-unavailable) since focus entry targets it as the only always-present control.","No new props, callbacks, state or npm dependencies for CitationModal or its callers; no focus trap, no inert/aria-hidden on background content; ChatArea.tsx and Message.tsx are not modified.","Dynamous citations never open the modal, so focus entry/return never applies to them.","Focus management survives React StrictMode's dev double-invoke (mount→cleanup→mount re-captures the correct opener) because opener capture, Close-button focus and restore all live in one empty-deps effect invocation paired with its own cleanup."],"modules":["CitationModal (app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx)"],"planned_files":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx"],"public_interfaces":["CitationModal(props: { citation: Citation; onClose: () => void }) -> JSX.Element (signature unchanged; focus management is internal)"],"seams":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect with cleanup: focus entry + focus return)","app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (document keydown Escape handler)","app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleCitationClick (chip activation opens CitationModal; Escape closes it)"],"version":"1.0"},"sha256":"b12a6976956859c6e8671faf313c3183da72f643b7badf40fad1b106dbbacd02","source":"design.json"},"frontier":{"content":{"accepted":true,"blockers":[{"issue":181,"state":"CLOSED"}],"issue":189,"ready":true,"ticket_sha256":"50959c913674f89ffb3c